cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "hep-endpoints: experiment-neutral adapters for HEP compute endpoints"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24418701"
authors:
  - family-names: Mina
    given-names: Rob
    affiliation: "University of Virginia"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2241-8566"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RobMina/hep-endpoints"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  hep-endpoints submits, tracks, fetches and cancels jobs on HEP compute endpoints (Slurm over SSH, FNAL Elastic Analysis Facility, FNAL jobsub_lite) behind one interface, with idempotent handles, durable submission intents, snapshots and artifact bindings.
keywords:
  - "workflow"
  - "Slurm"
  - "HTCondor"
  - "jobsub"
  - "HPC"
  - "particle physics"
